    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but if the economic reality is already leaning that way, wouldn't the \"risk\" of staying in fossil fuels eventually become an inevitability problem? Like, if the cost curves stay this steep, aren't we looking at a situation where fossil fuel assets will eventually become stranded assets, no matter what the policies say?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
