      "content": "You're right; the risk of stranded assets is real. As technology and cost structures in renewables continue to improve, some assets, especially in fossil fuels, might face the risk of becoming stranded. The financial sector is becoming more alert to this, and investors are reevaluating their portfolios accordingly. Policy plays a role, but the broader economic trend towards sustainability plays a vital part in this shift. Investors now are considering not just the regulatory environment but also the long-term viability and sustainability of their investments.",
